  "@walletInFlightNoteSyncPaused": {
    "description": "walletInFlightNote's variant when NO background sync pass will run (re-keyed and renamed by #403 R4). The second leg forwards only on sync passes, so 'still completing' would claim progress and then negate it — this variant says 'partway through … paused' as one coherent story. Renamed from ...SyncOff and made CAUSE-AGNOSTIC for the same reason as its three re-keyed siblings (walletParkedPreparingHintSyncPaused, walletParkedAuthorizeSentSyncPaused, walletParkedSyncPausedNote): the drive is also not running after a FAILED sync start, where the host policy still reads on and 'syncing is off in this app's settings' is simply the wrong remedy — the screen's own sync notice carries the cause. Match walletSyncPausedMoneyNote's condition wording. Keep the D2 'set aside' term and the identical don't-send-again instruction; same plural rule and placeholders as the sibling.",
